From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_ncm: Retry the flush of a partial NTB when no
 request is free

A partial NTB is sent by a timer once no further frame has joined it for
300 us. The timer calls eth_start_xmit() without a frame, which returns
NETDEV_TX_BUSY when every transmit request is still in flight. The return
value was ignored and the timer not restarted, so the frames already
packed stayed in the NTB until the network stack happened to send another
one. With a peer waiting for exactly those frames, a transfer stalled.

Restart the timer when the flush found no request. A suspended port
reports the same value and is left as before: nothing can be sent until
the host resumes the bus.

Assisted-by: LLM
[Orchard: from brkosebay/orchard f72349fc6 (OrchardLinux/orchard#109),
 tested there on a J71t with 157 MB and 164 MB transfers. Changed: the
 timer is not restarted while the port is suspended, where it would
 otherwise fire every 300 us until the host wakes; that case is
 untested on hardware.]
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
index bf02545b37a2..49972935961d 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_ncm.c
@@ -1158,7 +1158,15 @@ static enum hrtimer_restart ncm_tx_timeout(struct hrtimer *data)
 		 *
 		 * This will call directly into u_ether's eth_start_xmit()
 		 */
-		netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev);
+		if (netdev->netdev_ops->ndo_start_xmit(NULL, netdev) ==
+		    NETDEV_TX_BUSY && !READ_ONCE(ncm->port.is_suspend)) {
+			/*
+			 * No request was free, so the partial NTB was not
+			 * sent. Try again; a completion frees a request.
+			 */
+			hrtimer_forward_now(data, TX_TIMEOUT_NSECS);
+			return HRTIMER_RESTART;
+		}
 	}
 	return HRTIMER_NORESTART;
 }
